Chat 001 — AI-assisted scaffolding of Task Manager full-stack app
Tool: Claude Code (Claude, Anthropic)
Date: 2026-08-20

Purpose of AI use:
- Generate the initial Spring Boot 3 + Vue 3 project skeleton (directory layout, pom.xml,
  Vue/TS scaffold) instead of hand-typing boilerplate.
- Produce CRUD boilerplate (entity / repository / service / controller / DTOs on the backend;
  API client / components on the frontend) from a plain-language description of the required
  features (view / create / edit / mark complete-incomplete / delete tasks).
- Diagnose and fix a runtime dependency-compatibility issue (springdoc-openapi 2.6.0 threw
  NoSuchMethodError against Spring Boot 3.5.3 / Spring Framework 6.2.8; resolved by bumping
  springdoc to 2.8.6).
- Wire up OpenAPI documentation (springdoc) and verify it end-to-end with curl before writing
  this record.

Summary of exchange:
1. User asked how to publish this assignment's source code as a GitHub repository so an
   interviewer could review/run it. Assistant explained the end-to-end process (local project
   setup, GitHub repo creation, README/OpenAPI/domain-model documentation requirements, and the
   assignment's AI-usage disclosure rule) without making any changes yet.
2. User said "開始動手" (start building). Assistant asked three clarifying questions (project
   location, database choice, GitHub repo status) via a short Q&A, then:
   - Discovered start.spring.io no longer serves Spring Boot 3.x (only >=4.0.0 as of this date),
     so hand-wrote pom.xml pinned to the last Spring Boot 3.x GA release (3.5.3) to satisfy the
     assignment's explicit "Spring Boot 3" requirement.
   - Hand-wrote the backend: Task entity, TaskRepository, TaskService, TaskController (REST:
     GET/POST/PUT/PATCH .../complete/.../incomplete/DELETE under /api/tasks), TaskRequest/
     TaskResponse DTOs with bean validation, and a @RestControllerAdvice for 404/400 handling.
   - Configured H2 in-memory DB and springdoc-openapi for automatic OpenAPI/Swagger UI, on port
     8082 (chosen to avoid clashing with other local projects' 8080/8081 on this machine).
   - Scaffolded the frontend with `npm create vue@latest` (TypeScript, no router/pinia/vitest),
     removed the generated boilerplate (HelloWorld/TheWelcome/WelcomeItem/logo), and wrote
     TaskForm.vue / TaskList.vue / TaskItem.vue / App.vue plus a typed fetch-based API client
     (src/api/tasks.ts) and Task/TaskInput types. Added a Vite dev-server proxy for /api so the
     frontend can call the backend without CORS configuration.
   - Ran `mvn clean verify` (backend) and `npm run type-check && npm run build` (frontend) to
     confirm both sides are green.
   - Started both servers and smoke-tested the full CRUD flow, validation errors, 404 handling,
     and the OpenAPI docs / Swagger UI endpoints with curl; confirmed the Vite dev proxy
     correctly forwards /api/tasks to the backend.
   - Hit and fixed the springdoc/Spring Boot version mismatch described above.
3. Per the assignment's AI-usage instructions, added `// [AI assisted 001]` comments to the
   AI-generated source files and recorded this rationale in this chat-records/001.chat file.

